			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Convert Intercept proxies to async import, remove poll retry loops\n\nReplace synchronous `require()` with `await import()` across all six low-level Intercept proxies (AsyncProxy, CancellationProxy, DisposableProxy, EmitterFireProxy, ErrorHandlerProxy, TimingProxy), eliminating the 50-attempt × 100ms poll-based retry fallback in each. Since the activation sequence in `activateLowLevelHooks()` guarantees target modules are already loaded by the time these fire, dynamic import either resolves immediately or the proxy returns early.\n\nAlso: correct the ErrorHandlerProxy marker comment to `__LAND_SHIM_LOW_ERROR_HANDLER_PROXY__`, thread the `stopwatchModule` reference directly into TimingProxy's `patchStopWatch()` instead of re-requiring it, and add `Intercept/Index.ts` — a barrel file exporting all six proxies as default-exported async functions for unified import in the activation site.\n\nThis reduces boilerplate by ~120 lines of polling infrastructure and removes the last `require()` calls from the shim runtime, making the intercept layer fully ES-module-compatible.",
			"SHA": "fe9476e466ee4553f105ec9679a13675af46c6b1"
		},
