				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add unified LandDiagnostics tracer and wire low-level hooks into Init\n\nCreate `LandDiagnostics.ts`, a shared tracing pipeline that consolidates all shim hook reporting — both 🟠 low-level engine hooks (error, emitter, cancellation, disposable, async, timing) and 🔵 coverage-level audit entries. Each category gets a 512-entry ring buffer with a 30-second flush to Mountain via Tauri IPC `diagnostic:log`. Also adds `checkLandSwallowMap()` for fast event suppression (status bar and telemetry events) used by the Emitter.fire proxy.\n\nRefactor `Init.ts` to import `recordAuditEntry` and `forceFlush` from the new diagnostics module, replacing the local `recordAuditEntry` helper. Add `activateLowLevelHooks()` which dynamically imports all six Intercept proxy modules at `Own`/`Preempt` tiers — the runtime activation site for the low-level engine hooks added in ebe465d04. Restructure tier logic with clear 🔵 (coverage/Proxy/Replace) and 🟠 (low-level/Own/Preempt) sections.",
			"SHA": "df86a1f7314aea016d58e0fc919dbe3d2a608b0e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:17:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				355,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add six low-level intercept proxies for deep-shim Own/Preempt tiers\n\nIntroduce the runtime intercept layer — six proxy modules that monkey-patch VS Code internals at Startup/StartupServices time to provide Land-controlled diagnostics, suppression, and batching.\n\nAll six follow a consistent pattern:\n- Gate at TierShim = Own | Preempt (dead-code-eliminated by esbuild define otherwise)\n- Idempotent via globalThis marker (checks `__LAND_SHIM_LOW_*__`)\n- Poll-based retry (50 attempts × 100ms) if the target module is not yet loaded\n- Non-fatal error handling (try/catch everywhere — shim must never crash the workbench)\n\nProxies added:\n- AsyncProxy — intercepts `setTimeout0` from platform.ts with micro-batching (MAX_BATCH_SIZE=64), coalescing rapid microtasks to reduce layout thrash. Samples every 128th call for trace.\n- CancellationProxy — patches `CancellationTokenSource.prototype.cancel()` to record timestamp, stack trace, and cancellation order for diagnostic analysis.\n- DisposableProxy — wraps `DisposableStore.prototype.add()` and `dispose()` to assign unique tracking IDs and trace resource creation/disposal for leak detection.\n- EmitterFireProxy — intercepts `Emitter.prototype.fire()` from event.js, checks `checkLandSwallowMap` for event suppression, and applies sample-based tracing (1% production, 100% dev) via tick-counter throttle.\n- ErrorHandlerProxy — patches `errorHandler.onUnexpectedError()` to capture error message, stack, and name into LandErrorTrace before VS Code processes the error.\n- TimingProxy — wraps StopWatch construction, stop(), and elapsed() with microsecond-resolution timing via performance.now / process.hrtime fallback, uniquely identifying each instance.",
			"SHA": "ebe465d04fcdb4715f44e51a60dd16aa4dda4a93"
		},
