				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Wire InjectShimHook into the BuildPipeline plugin array\n\nRegister `InjectShimHook` in the `BuildPipeline` plugin sequence, slotting it immediately after `ExposeWorkbenchAccessor`. The hook is gated by the `TierShim` env var (None → no-op) and performs deep-shim injection — audit proxy, service replacement, or container ownership — depending on the configured shim level.\n\nThis completes the integration of the compile-time injection site (added in 9b81aa2c7) into the actual esbuild plugin pipeline that runs during Output builds. The shim init module (`CEL/Land/Shim/Init.js` from 07d07070f) is compiled, copied, and injected as part of `ApplyPipeline`; this wiring ensures the hook fires on every workbench build.\n\nSee: .hermes/microsoft/04-Atomic-Task-List.md",
